    <main class="container py-5">
        <div class="row">
            
  <div class="col-lg-8">
    <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="TGCET Results 2026 Declared">
    <div class="blog-content">
      <div class="blog-body">
        <h1 class="blog-title mb-4">TGCET Results 2026 OUT: Your Gateway to Gurukul Education is Here!</h1>

        <p class="lead mb-4">The moment thousands of students and parents across Telangana have been eagerly anticipating has arrived! The Telangana Gurukul Common Entrance Test (TGCET) 2026 results have been officially declared on March 24, 2026. This announcement marks a crucial step for students aspiring to secure admission into prestigious Gurukul residential schools for Classes 5 to 9 across the state.</p>

        <div class="highlight-text">
          <p>The TGCET 2026 examination, held on February 22, 2026, serves as a gateway to quality residential education offered by various welfare societies including TSWREIS, TTWREIS, MJPTBCWREIS, and TREIS.</p>
        </div>

        <p>The results, which include vital details like marks obtained, rank, and qualifying status, are now accessible online through the official portal. It's time to check your performance and prepare for the next stages of the admission process!</p>

        <h2 class="section-title">How to Check Your TGCET 2026 Results</h2>
        <p>Checking your TGCET 2026 scorecard is a straightforward process. Follow these simple steps to access your results online:</p>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official Website</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">Navigate to the official Telangana Gurukul Common Entrance Test (TGCET) website at <a href="https://tgcet.cgg.gov.in/" target="_blank">tgcet.cgg.gov.in</a>.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the Result Link</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, look for the prominent link that reads "TGCET 2026 Result" or "TG Gurukulam CET Result 2026". This link will typically be flashing or highlighted.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">3. Enter Your Credentials</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">Click on the result link and you will be redirected to a new page. Here, you will need to enter your Hall Ticket Number. Some portals might also require your Date of Birth.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">4. Submit and View Result</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">After entering the required details, click on the "Submit" button. Your TGCET 2026 result and digital scorecard will then be displayed on your screen.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">5. Download and Print Your Scorecard</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">It is highly recommended to download the PDF of your scorecard and take a printout for future reference and for the upcoming admission procedures.</div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="section-title">Key Details on Your TGCET 2026 Scorecard</h2>
        <p>The online scorecard is an essential document and contains critical information about your performance. Make sure to verify all the details carefully:</p>

        <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
          <p>✅ Candidate's Name</p>
          <p>✅ Hall Ticket Number</p>
          <p>✅ Marks Obtained</p>
          <p>✅ Rank (if applicable)</p>
          <p>✅ Category</p>
          <p>✅ Qualifying Status</p>
        </div>
        <p>In case of any discrepancies, it is crucial to contact the concerned authorities immediately to rectify the issue.</p>

        <h2 class="section-title">What's Next? The Post-Result Journey</h2>
        <p>The declaration of TGCET 2026 results is just the beginning. Qualified candidates will now proceed to the subsequent stages of the admission process. The final selection for admission will be based on merit and the rank secured in the entrance test, adhering to reservation criteria.</p>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">Certificate Verification</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">Shortlisted students will be invited for certificate verification. It is essential to have all original documents, such as caste certificate, income certificate, transfer certificate, bonafide certificates, and photographs, ready. The dates for document verification are expected to be notified within a week of the result announcement.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">Counselling Process</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">Following verification, a counselling schedule will be released by the respective conducting bodies (TSWREIS, TTWREIS, MJPTBCWREIS, TREIS). This is where candidates will be guided through the seat allotment process.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">Seat Allotment</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">Final admission to the Gurukul schools will be based on the candidate's rank, preference, reservation rules, and the availability of seats.</div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="section-title">Important Dates at a Glance</h2>
        <p>Stay informed about the critical dates related to TGCET 2026:</p>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Event</th>
              <th>Date</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>TGCET 2026 Exam Date</td>
              <td>February 22, 2026</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>TGCET 2026 Result Declaration</td>
              <td>March 24, 2026</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Counselling &amp; Document Verification</td>
              <td>To be announced shortly</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>Congratulations to all the students who have successfully cleared the TGCET 2026! This is a significant achievement that opens doors to quality education and a brighter future. For those who may not have achieved their desired outcome, remember that there are always alternative pathways to success. Keep an eye on the official website for all further updates regarding the admission process.</p>

        <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)</h2>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">Q1: What is the official website to check TGCET Result 2026?</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">The official website to check TGCET Result 2026 is <a href="https://tgcet.cgg.gov.in/" target="_blank">tgcet.cgg.gov.in</a>.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">Q2: For which classes are the TGCET Gurukul Results 2026 declared?</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">The results are for admission into Classes 5 to 9 in various Telangana Gurukul residential schools.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">Q3: What details are required to check the Telangana Gurukul CET Result 2026?</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">Candidates primarily need their Hall Ticket Number. In some cases, Date of Birth might also be required.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="benefit-item">
          <div class="benefit-title">Q4: What should I do after checking my TGCET 2026 result?</div>
          <div class="benefit-content">After checking your result, download and print your scorecard. Then, prepare for the next steps which include certificate verification, counselling, and seat allotment. Keep all your necessary documents ready.</div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

            
            
